  <!-- Deep Engineering Science Section -->
  <div class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 shadow-sm space-y-6 mb-12">
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-title-lg font-bold text-ink tracking-tight flex items-center gap-2">
        <svg class="w-6 h-6 text-teal-600" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19.428 15.428a2 2 0 00-1.022-.547l-2.387-.477a6 6 0 00-3.86.517l-.318.158a6 6 0 01-3.86.517L6.05 15.21a2 2 0 00-1.806.547M8 4h8l-1 1v5.172a2 2 0 00.586 1.414l5 5c1.26 1.26.367 3.414-1.415 3.414H4.828c-1.782 0-2.674-2.154-1.414-3.414l5-5A2 2 0 009 10.172V5L8 4z"></path>
        </svg>
        {d.scienceTitle}
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-1 leading-relaxed">
        {d.scienceSub}
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 text-xs md:text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-xl p-4">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-ink mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-teal-500"></span>
            1. Peek's Law & Townsend Corona Ionization
          </h3>
          <p>
            When a high voltage $V$ is applied to a sharp conductor (wire radius $r_0 \approx 0.1\text{ mm}$), the local surface electric field gradient exceeds the dielectric breakdown threshold of ambient air ($E_0 \approx 30\text{ kV/cm}$). According to Peek's empirical criterion:
          </p>
          <div class="my-2 p-2 bg-slate-900 text-teal-300 font-mono text-xs rounded-lg text-center overflow-x-auto">
            $$E_c = m \cdot g_0 \cdot \delta \cdot \left(1 + \frac{0.308}{\sqrt{\delta \cdot r_0}}\right)$$
          </div>
          <p>
            where $m$ is wire roughness (0.85–0.95), $\delta$ is relative air density, and $g_0 = 31\text{ kV/cm}$. Townsend electron avalanches produce intense unipolar space charge clouds ($N_2^+, O_2^+$ in positive corona; electrons and $O_2^-$ in negative corona).
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-xl p-4">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-ink mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-teal-500"></span>
            2. Electrohydrodynamic Body Force & Ionic Wind
          </h3>
          <p>
            As unipolar ions drift under the electrostatic field toward the grounded collector, they undergo billions of elastic collisions with neutral air molecules ($N_2, O_2$). This momentum transfer exerts an electrohydrodynamic body force $\mathbf{f}_{body}$ directly onto the fluid:
          </p>
          <div class="my-2 p-2 bg-slate-900 text-teal-300 font-mono text-xs rounded-lg text-center overflow-x-auto">
            $$\mathbf{f}_{body} = \rho_c \mathbf{E} - \frac{1}{2} E^2 \nabla \varepsilon + \frac{1}{2} \nabla \left[E^2 \rho \left(\frac{\partial \varepsilon}{\partial \rho}\right)_T\right]$$
          </div>
          <p>
            In uniform air, the Coulombic term $\rho_c \mathbf{E}$ dominates, generating a perpendicular bulk air jet known as the **corona ionic wind** ($v_{wind} \approx 2.5\text{ to }5.0\text{ m/s}$) with zero moving mechanical fan components.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-xl p-4">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-ink mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-teal-500"></span>
            3. Boundary Layer Disruption & Sherwood Mass Transfer
          </h3>
          <p>
            In conventional still-air or laminar drying, evaporation is choked by a stagnant, saturated vapor boundary layer adhering to the food surface. The impinging EHD ionic wind generates micro-turbulent vortices that strip this laminar layer:
          </p>
          <div class="my-2 p-2 bg-slate-900 text-teal-300 font-mono text-xs rounded-lg text-center overflow-x-auto">
            $$\text{Sh} = \frac{h_m \cdot L}{D_{AB}} = 2 + 0.6 \cdot \text{Re}^{1/2} \cdot \text{Sc}^{1/3}$$
          </div>
          <p>
            This increases the mass transfer Sherwood number ($\text{Sh}$) by 300% to 500%, accelerating the water evaporation flux $J_w = h_m (C_{sat} - C_\infty)$ at ambient room temperatures ($20^\circ\text{C}$ to $25^\circ\text{C}$).
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-xl p-4">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-ink mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-teal-500"></span>
            4. Arrhenius Thermal Kinetics & Vitamin C Preservation
          </h3>
          <p>
            Ascorbic acid degrades according to temperature-dependent first-order Arrhenius kinetics ($k = A \exp(-E_a / RT)$, $E_a \approx 65\text{ kJ/mol}$). Conventional convective hot air ($65^\circ\text{C}$) accelerates thermal oxidation, destroying 50–70% of vitamin C.
          </p>
          <div class="my-2 p-2 bg-slate-900 text-teal-300 font-mono text-xs rounded-lg text-center overflow-x-auto">
            $$C(t) = C_0 \cdot \exp(-k(T) \cdot t) \quad \text{with } k(22^\circ\text{C}) \ll k(65^\circ\text{C})$$
          </div>
          <p>
            By operating at ambient temperature, EHD maintains $k$ at negligible rates, achieving >95% ascorbic acid retention, intact anthocyanin color pigments, and un-ruptured cell cellular turgor.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Benchmarks Table Section -->
  <div class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 shadow-sm space-y-4">
    <h3 class="text-title-md font-bold text-ink tracking-tight flex items-center gap-2">
      <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-teal-600" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M3 10h18M3 14h18m-9-4v8m-7 0h14a2 2 0 002-2V8a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z"></path>
      </svg>
      {d.tableTitle}
    </h3>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border-collapse">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-hairline bg-surface text-ink font-semibold">
            <th class="p-3">Dehydration Technology</th>
            <th class="p-3">Operating Temp (°C)</th>
            <th class="p-3">Vitamin C Retention (%)</th>
            <th class="p-3">Specific Energy (MJ/kg H2O)</th>
            <th class="p-3">Drying Rate Factor</th>
            <th class="p-3">Sensory & Texture Quality</th>
            <th class="p-3">Regulatory Status</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline/60">
          {ehdData.dryingTechnologyBenchmarks.map((bench, idx) => (
            <tr class={idx === 0 ? "bg-teal-50/50 dark:bg-teal-950/20 font-medium text-ink" : "text-muted hover:bg-surface/50"}>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-ink flex items-center gap-1.5">
                {idx === 0 && <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-teal-500"></span>}
                {bench.technology}
              </td>
              <td class="p-3 font-mono">{bench.operatingTempC}</td>
              <td class="p-3 font-bold font-mono text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">{bench.ascorbicAcidRetentionPercent}</td>
              <td class="p-3 font-mono">{bench.specificEnergyConsumptionMjPerKg}</td>
              <td class="p-3">{bench.dryingTimeFactor}</td>
              <td class="p-3">{bench.sensoryColorAromaQuality}</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-[11px]">{bench.regulatoryStatus}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Client-Side Reactive Physics Engine -->
<script is:inline>
  (function initEhdSimulator() {
    const systemSelect = document.getElementById('ehd-system-select');
    const substrateSelect = document.getElementById('ehd-substrate-select');
    const polaritySelect = document.getElementById('ehd-polarity-select');
    const scrubberSelect = document.getElementById('ehd-scrubber-select');

    const voltageSlider = document.getElementById('ehd-voltage-slider');
    const standoffSlider = document.getElementById('ehd-standoff-slider');
    const tempSlider = document.getElementById('ehd-temp-slider');
    const timeSlider = document.getElementById('ehd-time-slider');

    const voltageVal = document.getElementById('ehd-voltage-val');
    const standoffVal = document.getElementById('ehd-standoff-val');
    const tempVal = document.getElementById('ehd-temp-val');
    const timeVal = document.getElementById('ehd-time-val');

    const outWind = document.getElementById('ehd-out-wind');
    const outAccel = document.getElementById('ehd-out-acceleration');
    const outVitC = document.getElementById('ehd-out-vitc');
    const outSec = document.getElementById('ehd-out-sec');
    const outBoundary = document.getElementById('ehd-out-boundary');
    const outOzone = document.getElementById('ehd-out-ozone');
    const statusBadge = document.getElementById('ehd-status-badge');
    const limitationText = document.getElementById('ehd-limitation-text');
    const mitigationText = document.getElementById('ehd-mitigation-text');

    if (!systemSelect || !voltageSlider) return;

    function recalculate() {
      const voltage = parseFloat(voltageSlider.value);
      const standoff = parseFloat(standoffSlider.value); // mm
      const temp = parseFloat(tempSlider.value); // °C
      const time = parseFloat(timeSlider.value); // min

      voltageVal.textContent = voltage.toFixed(1) + ' kV';
      standoffVal.textContent = standoff.toFixed(0) + ' mm';
      tempVal.textContent = temp.toFixed(0) + '°C';
      timeVal.textContent = time.toFixed(0) + ' min';

      const sysId = systemSelect.value;
      const subId = substrateSelect.value;
      const polId = polaritySelect.value;
      const scId = scrubberSelect.value;

      // Electric field in kV/cm: E = V / (d in cm)
      const gapCm = standoff / 10.0;
      const electricFieldKvPerCm = voltage / gapCm;

      // Corona onset threshold voltage
      const coronaOnsetKv = polId === 'negative_dc_corona' ? 14.0 : 16.5;
      const breakdownThresholdKvPerCm = 32.0; // Air dielectric breakdown

      const isBreakdown = electricFieldKvPerCm >= breakdownThresholdKvPerCm || sysId === 'compromised_arcing_high_voltage_skid';
      const isSubCorona = voltage < coronaOnsetKv;

      // 1. Ionic wind velocity (m/s)
      let windVelocity = 0.0;
      if (isBreakdown) {
        windVelocity = 1.2; // Collapsed into erratic sparks
      } else if (isSubCorona) {
        windVelocity = 0.1; // Sub-threshold, natural buoyancy only
      } else {
        const deltaV = voltage - coronaOnsetKv;
        const polarityFactor = polId === 'negative_dc_corona' ? 1.25 : 1.0;
        windVelocity = (Math.sqrt(deltaV) * 0.95 * (30.0 / standoff) * polarityFactor);
        windVelocity = Math.max(0.5, Math.min(5.2, windVelocity));
      }

      // 2. Drying rate acceleration vs still air
      let accelFactor = 1.0;
      if (isBreakdown) {
        accelFactor = 1.3;
      } else if (isSubCorona) {
        accelFactor = 1.05;
      } else {
        accelFactor = 1.0 + (windVelocity * 0.75);
      }

      // 3. Boundary layer reduction (%)
      let boundaryReduction = Math.min(85.0, (windVelocity / 4.5) * 75.0);
      if (isBreakdown) boundaryReduction = 20.0;

      // 4. Vitamin C (Ascorbic Acid) Retention (%)
      let baseRetention = 97.5;
      // Thermal penalty: above 25°C, retention decreases
      const thermalLoss = Math.max(0, (temp - 25.0) * 0.45 * (time / 60.0));
      let vitCRetention = baseRetention - thermalLoss;
      if (isBreakdown) {
        vitCRetention = 32.0; // Thermal spark scorches product
      } else if (subId === 'probiotic_alginate_microbeads') {
        vitCRetention = Math.max(65.0, 98.0 - Math.max(0, (temp - 22.0) * 0.8));
      }
      vitCRetention = Math.max(15.0, Math.min(99.0, vitCRetention));

      // 5. Specific Energy Consumption (MJ/kg H2O)
      let sec = 1.45 + (voltage * 0.02) + (time > 90 ? 0.35 : 0.0);
      if (isBreakdown) sec = 8.5; // High power loss in sparks

      // 6. Ambient Ozone Concentration (ppm)
      let rawOzoneMgH = 8.5;
      if (sysId === 'high_density_needle_matrix_skid') rawOzoneMgH = 28.0;
      if (sysId === 'cleanroom_blade_electrode_skid') rawOzoneMgH = 2.2;
      if (sysId === 'compromised_arcing_high_voltage_skid') rawOzoneMgH = 185.0;
      if (polId === 'negative_dc_corona') rawOzoneMgH *= 1.8;

      let destructionEff = 0.998; // Catalytic MnO2
      if (scId === 'single_pass_activated_carbon_scrubber') destructionEff = 0.965;
      if (scId === 'unscrubbed_open_canopy_defective') destructionEff = 0.15;

      const escapedOzoneMgH = rawOzoneMgH * (1.0 - destructionEff);
      let ozonePpm = (escapedOzoneMgH / 850.0) * 1.25;
      if (scId === 'unscrubbed_open_canopy_defective' || isBreakdown) {
        ozonePpm = Math.max(0.45, ozonePpm);
      }

      // Output DOM updates
      outWind.textContent = windVelocity.toFixed(2) + ' m/s';
      outAccel.textContent = accelFactor.toFixed(1) + 'x Faster';
      outVitC.textContent = vitCRetention.toFixed(1) + '%';
      outSec.textContent = sec.toFixed(2) + ' MJ/kg';
      outBoundary.textContent = '-' + boundaryReduction.toFixed(1) + '%';
      outOzone.textContent = ozonePpm.toFixed(3) + ' ppm';

      // Badge & Limitation Logic
      if (isBreakdown) {
        statusBadge.className = "px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold tracking-wide bg-red-100 text-red-800 dark:bg-red-950/80 dark:text-red-200 border border-red-300 dark:border-red-800";
        statusBadge.textContent = "CRITICAL HAZARD: DIELECTRIC SPARK BREAKDOWN";
        limitationText.textContent = "Severe Spark Arcing & Thermal Scorching (E > 32 kV/cm)";
        mitigationText.textContent = "EMERGENCY INTERLOCK TRIP: Increase standoff gap to ≥ 30 mm, reduce voltage to ≤ 32 kV, inspect wire cleanliness.";
      } else if (ozonePpm > 0.10) {
        statusBadge.className = "px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold tracking-wide bg-amber-100 text-amber-800 dark:bg-amber-950/80 dark:text-amber-200 border border-amber-300 dark:border-amber-800";
        statusBadge.textContent = "OSHA WARNING: EXHAUST OZONE EXCEEDED (> 0.10 ppm)";
        limitationText.textContent = "Workplace Ozone Emission Threshold Exceeded (OSHA 29 CFR § 1910.1000)";
        mitigationText.textContent = "Activate closed-loop catalytic MnO2-CuO destructor or reduce negative corona voltage.";
      } else if (isSubCorona) {
        statusBadge.className = "px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold tracking-wide bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 dark:bg-blue-950/80 dark:text-blue-200 border border-blue-300 dark:border-blue-800";
        statusBadge.textContent = "SUB-CORONA: INSUFFICIENT IONIZATION";
        limitationText.textContent = "Applied voltage below Townsend ionization onset threshold (V < V0)";
        mitigationText.textContent = "Increase applied potential above 18 kV to establish stable unipolar corona wind.";
      } else {
        statusBadge.className = "px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold tracking-wide bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-950/80 dark:text-emerald-200 border border-emerald-300 dark:border-emerald-800";
        statusBadge.textContent = "OPTIMAL NON-THERMAL EHD DRYING (FDA & OSHA COMPLIANT)";
        limitationText.textContent = "Boundary Layer Moisture Diffusion Controlled (Sherwood Sh = " + (12.0 + windVelocity * 1.8).toFixed(1) + ")";
        mitigationText.textContent = "Operating conditions balanced: high Vitamin C retention (>95%) and zero ozone workplace exposure.";
      }
    }

    // Event listeners
    [systemSelect, substrateSelect, polaritySelect, scrubberSelect, voltageSlider, standoffSlider, tempSlider, timeSlider].forEach(el => {
      el.addEventListener('input', recalculate);
      el.addEventListener('change', recalculate);
    });

    // Presets
    document.querySelectorAll('.ehd-preset-btn').forEach(btn => {
      btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const p = btn.dataset.preset;
        if (p === 'strawberry') {
          systemSelect.value = 'multi_wire_ground_mesh_skid';
          substrateSelect.value = 'sliced_fresh_strawberries';
          polaritySelect.value = 'positive_dc_corona';
          scrubberSelect.value = 'catalytic_mno2_cuo_recirculating';
          voltageSlider.value = 28.0;
          standoffSlider.value = 30;
          tempSlider.value = 22;
          timeSlider.value = 45;
        } else if (p === 'apple') {
          systemSelect.value = 'high_density_needle_matrix_skid';
          substrateSelect.value = 'raw_apple_slices';
          polaritySelect.value = 'negative_dc_corona';
          scrubberSelect.value = 'catalytic_mno2_cuo_recirculating';
          voltageSlider.value = 32.0;
          standoffSlider.value = 35;
          tempSlider.value = 25;
          timeSlider.value = 60;
        } else if (p === 'mushroom') {
          systemSelect.value = 'multi_wire_ground_mesh_skid';
          substrateSelect.value = 'shiitake_medicinal_mushrooms';
          polaritySelect.value = 'positive_dc_corona';
          scrubberSelect.value = 'catalytic_mno2_cuo_recirculating';
          voltageSlider.value = 26.0;
          standoffSlider.value = 40;
          tempSlider.value = 20;
          timeSlider.value = 90;
        } else if (p === 'probiotic') {
          systemSelect.value = 'cleanroom_blade_electrode_skid';
          substrateSelect.value = 'probiotic_alginate_microbeads';
          polaritySelect.value = 'positive_dc_corona';
          scrubberSelect.value = 'catalytic_mno2_cuo_recirculating';
          voltageSlider.value = 22.0;
          standoffSlider.value = 25;
          tempSlider.value = 18;
          timeSlider.value = 40;
        } else if (p === 'hazard') {
          systemSelect.value = 'compromised_arcing_high_voltage_skid';
          substrateSelect.value = 'sliced_fresh_strawberries';
          polaritySelect.value = 'negative_dc_corona';
          scrubberSelect.value = 'unscrubbed_open_canopy_defective';
          voltageSlider.value = 42.0;
          standoffSlider.value = 15;
          tempSlider.value = 35;
          timeSlider.value = 120;
        }
        recalculate();
      });
    });

    // Initial run
    recalculate();
  })();
</script>
